          "notes": "Address verbatim from user 2026-04-18. HART base for NWAS in Manchester is co-located at BTTG Testing & Certification Ltd. Covers the whole NWAS region, not just GM. Fleet reconciled 2026-09-02 against the NWAS HART vehicle register (FOI24474, 14 Apr 2025, 'Manchester Central' division = 12 vehicles: 8x MAN TGE 5.160, 1x Toyota Hilux, 1x DAF LF 45.170, 1x Polaris Ranger, 1x Skoda Kodiaq) and the vehicle-role descriptions NWAS gave in FOI24477 (9 Apr 2025). The 8 MAN TGEs split 5 IRU (3 live + 2 spare) + 2 personnel carriers (1 overt, 1 covert) + 1 multi-casualty; only the 3 live IRUs are modelled as mobilisable, so 10 units here against 12 on the register. This is the 3rd-generation NARU/NHS ECU national fleet, delivered Sep 2024 - Jan 2025. Callsigns use the published Z (HART) prefix from FOI2376; the 3xx block is enthusiast observation (Z301/Z304), not an NWAS disclosure - NWAS withholds callsign numbers under s24. Callsigns authored (U6): 4x HART_vehicle, 1x HART_ORIRU, 1x NWAS_IRU, 1x HART_ATV, 1x HART_RRV.",
